─────────────────────────────────────────
COMIC PANEL
─────────────────────────────────────────

IComicPanel
  │     int Rank
  │     LoopCount FirstLoop
  │     LoopCount LastLoop
  │     CinemachineBlendDefinition IncomingBlend
  │     bool HasBeenVisited
  │     UnityEvent OnPanelComplete      (raised when all steps done and panel is ready to exit)
  │     UnityEvent OnReadyForInput      (raised when the advance button should be enabled)
  │     void Show()                     (entry animation — forward story progression only)
  │     void ShowInstant()              (end state, no animation — history navigation only)
  │     void Replay()                   (reset + Show() — called by Replay button)
  │     void Hide()
  │     void Advance()
  └── ComicPanel  (MonoBehaviour — implements IComicPanel)
        │     [SerializeField] PanelDataSO data          (designer sets rank, loop, blend, etc.)
        │     [SerializeField] PlayerChoicesSO choices   (read at Activate() time per step)
        │     [SerializeField] CinemachineCamera cam     (child object; assigned in Inspector)
        │     [RequireComponent] Animator anim           (same GameObject; resolved via GetComponent in Awake)
        │     IPanelStep[] _steps                        (collected via GetComponentsInChildren in Awake)
        │     bool _isBlocked                            (starts true in Show(); cleared after intro completes)
        │
        │     Show()        ──►  enable cam+anim, deactivate all steps, _isBlocked=true,
        │                        play Intro (or skip to end if revisit), wait for completion
        │     ShowInstant() ──►  enable cam+anim, activate steps where ShowInFinalState=true,
        │                        snap Animator to end; does NOT fire OnReadyForInput
        │     Hide()        ──►  disable cam+anim, stop coroutine
        │     Replay()      ──►  PrepareForReplay() all steps, reset HasBeenVisited, call Show()
        │     Advance()     ──►  while loop: read IsBlocking BEFORE Activate(), activate step,
        │                        if blocking → lock input + register UnblockPanel listener;
        │                        if non-blocking → auto-chain to next step immediately;
        │                        fire OnPanelComplete when all steps processed
        │
        │     HasBeenVisited is set at the END of WaitForIntroCompletion() — not at the start of Show().
        │     (If set early, navigating away mid-animation leaves HasBeenVisited=true, causing the panel
        │      to skip to its end state on the next forward visit instead of replaying the animation.)
        │
        │     _isBlocked starts TRUE at the top of Show() — input must be locked from the moment
        │     the panel begins showing, before the intro animation finishes.
        │
        └── Steps  (children implementing IPanelStep, activated in hierarchy top-to-bottom order)
              ├── AnimatedStep     — plays an animation clip; optional focus-variant PanelText children
              ├── MiniGame         — abstract; subclass for each puzzle (e.g. SignalGame)
              └── FocusPoint       — STUB; will write a choice to PlayerChoicesSO (see AGENTS.md)

─────────────────────────────────────────
IPANELSTEP CONTRACT
─────────────────────────────────────────

IPanelStep
  │     bool IsBlocking         — if true, Advance() locks input after Activate() until OnStepComplete fires
  │     bool ShowInFinalState   — if true, ShowInstant() calls Activate(); otherwise calls Deactivate()
  │     UnityEvent OnStepComplete
  │     void Activate(PlayerChoicesSO choices)
  │     void Deactivate()
  │     void PrepareForReplay()

ShowInFinalState MUST combine designer intent with runtime state:
  AnimatedStep:  ShowInFinalState => persistsInFinalState && _hasBeenActivated
  MiniGame:      ShowInFinalState => false  (puzzles never persist in history view)

The _hasBeenActivated guard is NOT optional. Calling Activate() on a step that has never been
through Advance() plays its animation outside the blocking system, permanently locking the
advance button because UnblockPanel is never registered as a listener.

─────────────────────────────────────────
STEPBASE
─────────────────────────────────────────

StepBase  (abstract MonoBehaviour — shared base for all IPanelStep implementations)
  │     bool replayOnRevisit    — controls loop-revisit behaviour ONLY (not the Replay button)
  │     bool hideOnRevisit      — controls loop-revisit behaviour ONLY (not the Replay button)
  │     bool _hasBeenActivated  — private; read via HasBeenActivated (protected)
  │     bool IsBlocking         ── !_hasBeenActivated || replayOnRevisit
  │                                MUST be read BEFORE calling Activate() — Activate() calls
  │                                BeginActivation() which sets _hasBeenActivated=true, changing
  │                                IsBlocking for steps with replayOnRevisit=false. Reading after
  │                                Activate() incorrectly treats first-visit steps as non-blocking,
  │                                causing the auto-chain loop to fire two steps simultaneously.
  │     PrepareForReplay()      ── unconditionally resets _hasBeenActivated=false so the Replay
  │                                button always replays all steps. Override in subclasses that
  │                                should preserve state (e.g. FocusPoint keeps its chosen option).
  │     BeginActivation()       ── sets _hasBeenActivated=true; returns skip=true on loop revisit
  │                                when replayOnRevisit=false
  └── Loop-revisit behaviour (replayOnRevisit / hideOnRevisit) affects BeginActivation() only.
      Explicit replay (Replay button) always resets via PrepareForReplay(); flags are irrelevant.

Loop-revisit modes (only apply during story-forward Show() on a previously visited panel):
  replayOnRevisit=true,  hideOnRevisit=—     → full animation replay; blocks input
  replayOnRevisit=false, hideOnRevisit=false → snaps to final frame; auto-chained, no advance press
  replayOnRevisit=false, hideOnRevisit=true  → stays hidden; auto-chained, no advance press

─────────────────────────────────────────
ANIMATEDSTEP
─────────────────────────────────────────

AnimatedStep  (sealed MonoBehaviour — extends StepBase)
  │     [SerializeField] bool persistsInFinalState
  │     [RequireComponent] Animator _anim           (resolved via GetComponent in Awake)
  │     ShowInFinalState => persistsInFinalState && HasBeenActivated
  │
  │     Activate(choices):
  │       skip = BeginActivation()
  │       !skip           → populate PanelText children, SetActive(true), SeekAnimator(0f)
  │       skip && !hide   → SetActive(true), SeekAnimator(1f)  [frozen/final state]
  │       skip && hide    → stay deactivated; IsBlocking=false; Advance() auto-chains
  │
  │     SeekAnimator(normalizedTime):
  │       Update(0f)                              — resolve Entry→default-state transition
  │       GetCurrentAnimatorStateInfo(0).fullPathHash — read hash at runtime; designers name
  │                                                     states freely, no static hash possible
  │       Play(hash, 0, normalizedTime)
  │       Update(0f)                              — evaluate Animator at target time
  │
  │     OnAnimationFinished()  — Animation Event on last keyframe; calls OnStepComplete.Invoke()
  │     Reset()                — called by Unity on component add: SetActive(false), replayOnRevisit=true
  │
  └── PanelText  (child MonoBehaviour — focus-variant text display)
        Animator controls visibility. Holds variant text strings per choice combination.
        Populate(choices) selects the correct string at activation time.

