─────────────────────────────────────────
KEY DESIGN DECISIONS
─────────────────────────────────────────

• PlayerChoicesSO decouples all systems — no class needs a ComicManager reference
  just to know what the player chose. All panels share one asset via [SerializeField].

• PanelDataSO lets non-programmers add/configure panels entirely in the Inspector.
  Name assets Panel_01_, Panel_02_ … so Project window sort = comic order.

• lastLoop on PanelDataSO (default Loop3) retires panels without any code change —
  set it lower on the asset to stop a panel appearing after a specific loop.
  Panel eligibility logic lives solely in PanelSelector.

• LoopCountBounds.Last replaces hardcoded LoopCount.Loop4 — derived automatically from
  the enum via Enum.GetValues, so adding a new loop value requires only one file change.

• CommandHistory (two stacks) replaces CommandQueue — correct structure for undo/redo.
  Undo/Redo use ShowInstant(); Execute uses Show() — history never replays animations.

• IComicPanel hides Unity types — interface uses Show()/Hide()/UnityEvent, testable
  without Cinemachine/Animator dependencies.

• IPanelStep ShowInFinalState puts both guards (designer flag + runtime activated) inside
  the implementor — ShowInstant() asks one question, gets one answer.

• HasBeenVisited set at end of WaitForIntroCompletion() — navigating away mid-animation
  leaves HasBeenVisited false so the animation replays correctly on the next visit.

• _isBlocked starts true in Show() — input is blocked from the moment the panel begins
  showing, before the intro animation finishes, preventing premature step activation.

• IsBlocking is read BEFORE Activate() in ComicPanel.Advance() — Activate() calls
  BeginActivation() which sets _hasBeenActivated=true, changing IsBlocking post-call for
  steps with replayOnRevisit=false. Reading after would incorrectly treat first-visit
  steps as non-blocking, causing the auto-chain loop to fire two steps simultaneously.

• Advance() auto-chains non-blocking steps in a single burst (while loop, not if/else) —
  on revisit, all frozen/hidden steps appear on one advance press without individual presses.
  The loop terminates at: a blocking step, the last step, or OnPanelComplete.

• PrepareForReplay() unconditionally resets _hasBeenActivated — the Replay button always
  replays every step regardless of replayOnRevisit / hideOnRevisit. Those flags are loop-
  revisit only. Subclasses override PrepareForReplay() to preserve state (e.g. FocusPoint).

• replayOnRevisit / hideOnRevisit flags control loop-revisit behaviour via BeginActivation()
  only — not the Replay button. Two bools (not an enum) serialise cleanly as Inspector
  checkboxes and avoid serialisation migration if names change.

• CanvasGroup alpha + blocksRaycasts for NavigationPresenter button visibility — never
  SetActive(false) on Animator-driven buttons; re-enabling restarts the Animator from its
  Entry state, causing a flash of the default state on every show.

• NavigationController unblocks input ONLY via OnPanelReadyForInput — the prior
  OnCameraActivated (Cinemachine blend complete) approach caused a race condition where
  the blend could finish before the panel's intro animation, unlocking input prematurely.

• InputAction.performed callback replaces Update() polling in NavigationController.

• CursorMode.ForceSoftware in CursorTrigger and CursorManager — required on macOS;
  hardware cursors are intercepted by the OS in the Editor.

• [RequireComponent(typeof(Animator))] on ComicPanel and AnimatedStep — Animator is always
  co-located on the same GameObject, resolved via GetComponent in Awake, not [SerializeField].
  Prevents accidental removal and eliminates one manual wiring step per variant.

─────────────────────────────────────────
SCENE SETUP FOR A PANEL
─────────────────────────────────────────

IMPORTANT — Animator placement rule:
  An Animator can only animate objects within its own GameObject's subtree (itself + descendants).
  The panel Animator MUST be on the ComicPanel ROOT so it can reach all children.
  If the Animator is on a child, it cannot animate siblings, parents, or the root.

ComicPanel_XX_Name (GameObject)          ← ComicPanel.cs + Animator live HERE (root)
  ├── CinemachineCamera                  ← one per panel; starts disabled automatically
  ├── Step_01_Reveal                     ← AnimatedStep (first spacebar press)
  ├── Step_02_Dialogue                   ← AnimatedStep with PanelText child(ren) (second press)
  ├── Step_03_SpriteIn                   ← AnimatedStep, purely visual (third press)
  └── Step_04_Puzzle                     ← MiniGame subclass (fourth press — blocks until complete)

Steps activate in hierarchy top-to-bottom order. Reorder by dragging GameObjects in the Hierarchy.
CinemachineCamera starts disabled by Awake(); ComicManager.Start() enables the first panel via Show().

─────────────────────────────────────────
SET UP AN ANIMATED STEP
─────────────────────────────────────────

1. Add a child GameObject to the ComicPanel root.
2. Add AnimatedStep — Animator is added automatically via [RequireComponent].
3. Create an animation clip; set it as the Animator's default state; disable Loop Time.
4. On the last keyframe, add an Animation Event → Function: OnAnimationFinished
5. The step blocks input until that event fires, then the next advance press is accepted.

Optional focus-variant text: add one or more child GameObjects with a PanelText component.
Use AnimatedStep's Animator to control when each text element appears. Fill in variant text
fields on each PanelText for each choice combination; empty fields fall back to defaultText.

Persists In Final State: tick this on any AnimatedStep that should remain visible when the
player browses history (UI arrows). Only steps already triggered via Advance() will show —
steps not yet reached are always hidden regardless of this setting (ShowInFinalState guard).

Loop-revisit behaviour (does NOT affect the Replay button — that always replays everything):
  Replay On Revisit ✅, Hide On Revisit —     → full animation replays, blocks input
  Replay On Revisit ☐,  Hide On Revisit ☐    → snaps to final frame; no advance press needed
  Replay On Revisit ☐,  Hide On Revisit ✅   → stays hidden entirely; no advance press needed

Save step children as inactive in Prefab Mode before saving — prevents TMP "No Font Asset"
warnings during Editor load. AnimatedStep.Reset() does this automatically for new components.

